A revoke that took the capability it was made through goes on,
so made again after a stop it fails, where a revoke never stopped went on to the end.
A call that stops leaves its caller the capability it was made through.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call stopped where its caller cannot make it again

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -247,7 +247,7 @@ bool cap_revoke_below(struct cap *root, const struct cap *through, bool preempt)
          * or the capability it was made through ends there:
          * the caller could not make the call again, so an interrupt must not decide how far it got.
          */
-        if (thread_table(current) == NULL || through->type == CAP_NONE) {
+        if (thread_table(current) == NULL || through == NULL) {
             return true;
         }
         if (root->child != 0 && cap_stop_here(preempt)) {
